course: dictionary
lesson: 10484
title: Turf: grass, soil and home ground
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Turf is a word with more than one meaning, so the sentence tells you which meaning to use. Its simplest meaning is short grass together with the layer of soil and roots underneath it.
explain: «The Inuit of the Arctic hunted seals and whales... and in winter some built snow houses called igloos, but most did not live in igloos all year; they also lived in houses of stone, turf and skins.» Here turf is the grass and soil cut and used as a building material, next to stone and skins.
explain: Turf can also be a place you feel you belong. «Home turf» means the place a person or team knows well and feels strong in. Context is the clue: if the sentence talks about a team's ground or a street someone knows, turf probably means that special place.
fact: Turf means short grass and the layer of soil and roots under it.
fact: A square of turf can be laid on the ground to make a lawn.
fact: «Home turf» means a place you know well and feel strong in, such as a team's home ground.
fact: «Turf out» is informal and means to throw someone or something out roughly.
fact: Horse racing in general is sometimes called «the turf».
exercise: «The Inuit of the Arctic... lived in houses of stone, turf and skins.» What else were these houses made from, apart from stone and skins? | *Turf | Glass | Gold
exercise: Leo shouts, «This is my turf, so get off it!» What does turf mean here? | *The place Leo feels he belongs and has a right to | A small piece of soil for planting seeds | A type of horse race | Soft green grass for playing on
exercise: Find and copy the word in «houses of stone, turf and skins» that names the same kind of thing as stone. | skins | Arctic | houses | *turf
test: What does «turf out» mean? | To plant new grass | To dig up soil slowly | *To throw someone out roughly | To win a race
test: A new lawn can be made by laying what? | Sand | Dead leaves | Bricks | *Squares of turf
exam: What does «home turf» mean? | *A place you know well and feel strong in | A type of car | A place you have never visited | A dark, muddy hole
